# ALLOWLIST: the build context is only what installing the package needs.
# Everything else is excluded first, so a stray local file - a NONMEM or other
# license file, an .env, a token in .Renviron, credentials, a check tree - can
# never reach an image, whatever sits in the checkout. (The RStudio image keeps
# the whole context at /opt/ferx; the slim image installs everything under
# inst/.) Add a path here only if `R CMD INSTALL` needs it.
# .github/workflows/docker.yml also scans every built image for secrets.
*

!DESCRIPTION
!NAMESPACE
!LICENSE
!LICENSE.md
!INDEX
!NEWS.md
!R/
!man/
!inst/
!src/

# Inside the allowed directories: local build output and generated files.
src/rust/target/
src/rust/.cargo/
src/rust/vendor/
src/rust/vendor.tar.xz
src/rust/vendor-config.toml
src/rust/vendor-Cargo.lock
src/rust/rust-toolchain.toml
src/*.o
src/*.so
src/*.dll
inst/doc/

# Never, anywhere below an allowed directory (belt and braces for files the
# allowlist above would otherwise let through).
**/.Renviron
**/.Rprofile
**/.Rhistory
**/.RData
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/.netrc
**/.git-credentials
**/.npmrc
**/*.lic
**/*.pem
**/*.key
**/*.p12
**/*.pfx
**/id_rsa*
**/id_ed25519*
**/.git
**/.DS_Store
